 ### Looks and materials (`FDiegeticScreenLook`, `EDiegeticMaterialMode`, `DiegeticScreenMaterial.*`)
 - **Material** (`MaterialMode`): **Automatic** (new screens) = the plugin's own materials, picked per variant (`EDiegeticMaterialVariant`, `GetWantedVariant`): **Glass** when the look blurs (Background Blur > 0) or the widget holds Background Blur widgets (and Blur Background Blur Widgets is on), else **Opaque** for Blend Mode Opaque, else **Panel**. **Engine Default** = the Widget Component's own (a plugin material left in Materials is removed). **Custom** = Materials element 0, look parameters still handed over. Screens saved before v2 load as Engine Default (custom version `DiegeticScreenVer` 1, `PostLoad`), so nothing changes under them.
-- **Materials** (made by the editor, `DiegeticScreenMaterial::Get` / `MakeMissing`): `M_DiegeticScreen`, `_Glass`, `_Opaque` in `/NameTBD/Diegetic` (the plugin's Content, when the plugin is the project's and writable; else `/Game/NameTBD/Diegetic`, the settings' paths updated and a warning to cook it). Made on the next tick after a screen first asks (never inside a registration), saved, every registered screen refreshed (`RefreshMaterial`); rebuilt in place when their `DiegeticMaterialVersion` parameter is older than the builder's (2). A packaged game loads them by the settings' paths (`UDiegeticUISettings::ScreenMaterial` / `GlassScreenMaterial` / `OpaqueScreenMaterial`, warning once when missing); the plugin's `Config/DefaultGame.ini` always cooks `/NameTBD/Diegetic`, and screens saved in levels reference them through Materials too.
+- **Materials** (made by the editor, `DiegeticScreenMaterial::Get` / `MakeMissing`): `M_DiegeticScreen`, `_Glass`, `_Opaque` in `/NameTBD/Diegetic` (the plugin's Content, when the plugin is the project's and writable; else `/Game/NameTBD/Diegetic`, the settings' paths updated and a warning to cook it). Made (v2_fix1) once the editor is idle after a screen first asks - a 0.25 s ticker waiting while anything is dragged (placing an actor from Place Actors: making, compiling and saving assets mid drag-drop froze the editor with no log), a transaction is open, a slow task runs, a game plays in the editor, packages load or garbage is collected (`CanMakeNow`); each variant at most once a session (`bMadeThisSession` - a failure is logged, never retried in a loop); compiled as an edit is (`PreEditChange` / `PostEditChange`, shaders in the background, no blocking slow task); saved straight to disk (`UPackage::SavePackage`, no dialogs or source-control prompts; a read-only file is warned about); then every registered screen refreshed (`RefreshMaterial`). Rebuilt in place when their `DiegeticMaterialVersion` parameter node (read off the graph, not the compiled parameter data, which lags a fresh build) is older than the builder's (2). Until made, screens draw with the engine's material. Screens ask on every registration (a dragged actor re-registers every frame), so the editor only finds loaded objects then; the disk is looked at once per variant (`bSearchedMissing`), and the provider never falls back to loading by path. A packaged game loads them by the settings' paths (`UDiegeticUISettings::ScreenMaterial` / `GlassScreenMaterial` / `OpaqueScreenMaterial`, warning once when missing); the plugin's `Config/DefaultGame.ini` always cooks `/NameTBD/Diegetic`, and screens saved in levels reference them through Materials too.
 - **Matching UMG:** surface, unlit, **AlphaComposite** (premultiplied - Slate draws into the transparent-black render target premultiplied; the engine's Translucent widget materials multiply by alpha twice, which darkens soft edges and glass panes), emissive x (1 / Eye Adaptation) by **IgnoreSceneExposure** (1 = auto exposure undone), translucency **after DOF** (Glass: before, where Scene Color is read), **Responsive AA**, no vertex fog. Two-sided with the back face hidden in the graph (`TwoSidedSign`) unless the screen is Two Sided (`ShowBackFace`), so one material serves both. The tonemapper still applies (see Still open).
 - **Look parameters** (Screen custom node, widget sampled with `SampleLevel 0` - the render target has no mips): Preset (`EDiegeticLookPreset`: Clean, Terminal (Green), Terminal (Amber), Hologram, Frosted Glass, LCD Panel, Custom - `MakePreset`; picking one in the Details or `SetLookPreset` sets the values), Brightness, IgnoreSceneExposure, PhosphorColor + Monochrome, Glow + GlowRadius (16 taps, in widget pixels), ScanlineIntensity / Count / Speed, RollingBar, Curvature, ChromaticAberration, Vignette, Flicker (24 Hz), Noise, PixelGrid (RGB sub-pixel stripes per widget pixel), Hologram: Additive (opacity scaled down - AlphaComposite with low opacity adds light), EdgeFade (camera vector . vertex normal), Glitch (rows jump). Set by the screen: ScreenPixels (Draw Size), ShowBackFace, UVRegion (Mesh Surface), BlurRegion0..7 / BlurShape0..7 / BlurRegionCount.
 - **Background blur** (Glass): Blur Setup custom node works out a radius (Background Blur over the whole screen, or each Background Blur widget's radius inside its rounded rectangle - signed distance) in widget pixels -> screen pixels (`ddx`/`ddy` of the widget-pixel position) -> view UV (View Size); 12 Scene Color taps (Coordinates mode, a golden-angle spiral) averaged; tinted toward GlassTint by its alpha (by luminance), x BlurBrightness; added under the widget's transparent parts (`Color += Behind * (1 - Alpha) * Mask`, `Alpha += (1 - Alpha) * Mask`). Scene Color is the opaque scene only (no other translucency behind).
